{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795610331,"nonce":"YVhkRmyA4mRSznuQ2UOKyROY+Rk=","title":"Text in a clip of its own fades at that clip's edges","message":"Inside an element with `overflow-fade`, text whose own ancestor also clips (a button, a cell) fades at that inner clip's edges: glyphs carry the fade distances but no fade rectangle, so the shader measures from the merged clip.\n\nShapes and SVGs were fixed in 1fef957ec658ed34d0dcec68309784beef79e9d274c1ff65f92e134a02c6f28d by carrying the fading node's own box. Glyphs need the same: a fade rect on `GpuGlyph` and in the text shader, filled from the rect `node_content` already has.\n\nAlso left there: an SVG reached by two fading edges takes only the stronger one.","files":null}]}